            <div class="callout info">
                <strong>Key Finding:</strong> The world has seen a modest long-term decline in homicide rates, with the global mean dropping from 8.3 (1990s) to 7.7 (2020s). However, this aggregate improvement masks stark regional disparities—the Americas consistently record rates 10-20x higher than Europe or Asia.
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- GLOBAL OVERVIEW -->
        <section id="global-overview">
            <h2>1. Global Homicide Rate Overview</h2>
            <p>The global trend in intentional homicide rates reveals a generally declining pattern over the 34-year observation period, though with significant fluctuations and regional variation. The median homicide rate across all reporting countries provides a robust central tendency measure that is less influenced by extreme outliers than the mean.</p>

            <div class="chart-container">
                <img src="chart1_global_trend.png" alt="Global Homicide Rate Trend 1990-2023">
                <p class="chart-title">Figure 1: Global intentional homicide rate trend showing median and mean rates from 1990 to 2023. The median provides a more robust measure of central tendency, less affected by extreme values.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="two-col">
